-- title:
--   Unique maximal ideal over a supersingular place (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q=3$, a nonzero level $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A,M')$ over the residue field $\kappa_A =$ `ResidueField A`, assumed to consist exactly of the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with value of the geometric $j$-invariant in `ssJSet`). Assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of the geometric level-$M'$ function field along $A$, compatible with coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series with coefficients in $A$. Further data: an element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$; an index $\zeta$ for primitive $q$-th roots of unity; families $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$, subject to: the explicit description of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ at the line at infinity as the ring of quotients of coefficient-reductions of Laurent series over $A$, transitivity of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-action via `levelAutBar` on the $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}\ell$ together with injectivity and permutation of this family under all `levelAutBar`; for $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$: contraction to $A$ on constants, invariance under all `levelAutBar` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, the property that each $f$ in $R_0$-integers which is regular wherever $\hat\jmath$ is and whose $R_0$-reduction lies in the valuation ring of $s$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}s$, with $f-a$ in the maximal ideal whenever the residue of $a \in A$ is the value at $s$ of that reduction, and the existence of $t \in O_{\mathrm{SS}}s$ with $t-a$ a unit for all $a \in A$. Finally, a subfield $K_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}/K_0$ algebraic and $\pi \in K_0$; a henselian discrete valuation domain $A_0$ with an injective local homomorphism $\iota : A_0 \to A$ whose image is $A \cap K_0$, inducing a surjection onto $\kappa_A$; a generator $\varpi_0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ with $\iota\varpi_0 = \pi$; the subfield $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, containing the image $\hat\jmath$ of $j$, nonzero there, with an $A_0$-algebra structure on $F_0$ induced by $\iota$. Then for each $s \in W$ there is a maximal ideal $\mathfrak n_s$ of `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A₀ F₀ ĵ`, the algebra of elements of $F_0$ integral over $A_0[\hat\jmath]$, such that the image of $\varpi_0$ lies in $\mathfrak n_s$; an element $g$ of that algebra lies in $\mathfrak n_s$ precisely when its image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}s$; and $\mathfrak n_s$ is the only maximal ideal $\mathfrak n$ containing $\varpi_0$ with the property that for every $f$ in $R_0$-integers regular wherever $\hat\jmath$ is whose reduction lies in the valuation ring of $s$, and every $a \in A_0$ whose residue is the value at $s$ of that reduction, every $g$ of the chart algebra equal to $f - \iota a$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $\mathfrak n$.
--
--   This is the statement that the fibre of the descended two-chart integral model over a supersingular place of the level-$M'$ floor consists of a single closed point, the contracted Drinfeld point, identified as the centre in the finite chart algebra of the Drinfeld valuation ring $O_{\mathrm{SS}}s$. It is the $q=3$ case of the corresponding step of the Igusa-tower leg of the semistable-covering construction, and feeds the statement assembling these points for $j$-values in `ssJSet`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_isMaximal_mem_iff_mem_maximalIdeal_drinfeldRing_unique_chartAlgFin_descent_of_eq_three.lean

